{#- Decision call (forfeit layer) user message — decision-first flow.

     Rendered as the FIRST LLM call of every turn when
     ``ExperimentConfig.use_split_forfeit_layer=True`` (2026-09-04 reorder;
     before that date the decision call ran after the task call). Its job
     is narrow: show the agent its accumulated session context and the
     forfeit menu, then collect CHOICE (+ REASON digit on FORFEIT). The
     task call runs afterwards, and only if the agent CONTINUEd.

     Nothing about the current round is shown here — not the stimulus and
     not any task reasoning — so ``ri_forfeit`` (the decision call's
     thinking tokens) measures continue/forfeit deliberation alone.

     Session context is controlled by
     ``ForfeitLayerConfig.split_context_level``: the caller passes the
     cumulative history block as ``user_body`` under ``"medium"`` /
     ``"full"`` and an empty string under ``"minimal"``.

     The caller (``UnifiedTurnManager``) is responsible for formatting the
     forfeit menu (``forfeit_layer/menu.j2``) and passing it in as
     ``menu_text``.

     Variables:
       user_body       : optional session context (history block); empty
                         string safe.
       menu_text       : str — pre-rendered forfeit menu block.
       forfeit_allowed : bool — gates the CHOICE/REASON schema.
-#}
{%- if user_body -%}
{{ user_body }}

{% endif -%}
A new round is about to begin. Before it is shown to you, decide — using your accumulated experience (Previous Turn Results above, if present) — whether to continue or forfeit.

{{ menu_text }}

=== Response Format ===
Respond with all of the following fields, each on its own line, in the order shown:

CHOICE: {% if forfeit_allowed %}<CONTINUE or FORFEIT>{% else %}CONTINUE{% endif %}
{% if forfeit_allowed %}REASON: <required only if CHOICE is FORFEIT — a single digit 1, 2, or 3 as listed in the menu>
{% endif %}
